      ],
      "focus": null,
      "checkpoint": {
        "question": "The bigger surface surrounds the same charge. The flux through it...",
        "type": "choice",
        "choices": [
          "doubles",
          "stays the same",
          "halves"
        ],
        "answer": 1,
        "tolerance": null,
        "unit": null,
        "hint": "Count the lines that cross the bigger bubble.",
        "reexplain_hint": "Use the count-the-lines picture again: every line that crosses the small bubble also crosses the big one."
      },
      "sliders": [],
      "warning": null,
      "audio_url": "/audio/20e452f681c2b8f02952214df1626de7c56540542e03f8bb66bb9a83dca2b7af.mp3"
    }
  },
  {
    "event": "step",
    "data": {
      "id": "s6",
      "kind": "explain",
      "say": "Same lines, same flux. Flux depends only on the charge inside: phi equals Q over epsilon zero. For three nanocoulombs, that is about 339 newton meters squared per coulomb.",
      "subtitles": {
        "uz": "Chiziqlar bir xil, oqim ham bir xil. Oqim faqat ichkaridagi zaryadga bog'liq: fi Q ni epsilon nolga bo'linganiga teng. Uch nanokulon uchun bu taxminan 339 N·m²/C.",
        "ru": null
      },
      "draw": [
        {
          "id": "eps-label",
          "color": null,
          "at": 0.0,
          "label": null,
          "group": null,
          "type": "text",
          "x": 790.0,
          "y": 430.0,
          "text": "ε₀ = 8.85 × 10⁻¹² C²/(N·m²)",
          "size": null
        },
        {
          "id": "sym-eps",
          "color": null,
          "at": 0.15,
          "label": null,
          "group": null,
          "type": "symbol",
          "x": 60.0,
          "y": 180.0,
          "symbol": "\\varepsilon_0",
          "meaning": "permittivity of free space",
          "unit": "C²/(N·m²)"
        },
        {
          "id": "formula",
          "color": null,
          "at": 0.3,
          "label": null,
          "group": null,
          "type": "math",
          "x": 790.0,
          "y": 510.0,
          "latex": "\\Phi = \\dfrac{Q}{\\varepsilon_0}",
          "size": 40.0
        },
        {
          "id": "example",
          "color": null,
          "at": 0.65,
          "label": null,
          "group": null,
          "type": "math",
          "x": 790.0,
          "y": 610.0,
          "latex": "Q = 3\\ \\text{nC} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\Phi \\approx 338.8\\ \\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}^2/\\text{C}",
          "size": null
        }
      ],
      "focus": null,
      "checkpoint": null,
      "sliders": [],
      "warning": null,
      "audio_url": "/audio/d79599622a6b0c6cb70b56627a5ea832b33589fb0edf1935af073bd51cbc351a.mp3"
    }
  },
  {
    "event": "step",
    "data": {
      "id": "s7",
      "kind": "summary",
      "say": "To sum up: flux counts field lines through a closed surface. Any closed surface around the same charge gives the same flux, Q over epsilon zero.",
      "subtitles": {
        "uz": "Xulosa: oqim yopiq sirtdan o'tgan maydon chiziqlarini sanaydi. Shu zaryad atrofidagi har qanday yopiq sirt bir xil oqim beradi: Q ni epsilon nolga bo'lingani.",
        "ru": null
